[h1]Island Airfields - Multiplayer Update[/h1]
Planes and helicopters can land on captured island airfields, receive hangar service and take off again on a new order.

[h2]What's new in 2.0.0 client beta[/h2]
[list]
[*]Host-side Lua gameplay using the shared CC2X SDK. The mod contains no private native plugin.
[*]Landing requests use the game's normal waypoint channel. The host validates aircraft and island ownership.
[*]New move/clear orders immediately cancel deferred landing requests. Full queues report rejection.
[*]Planes share the runway; helicopters use their own landing areas.
[*]Your airfields are shown immediately in team colour. Flying over your own islands again is unnecessary.
[*]Session changes clear old requests and flight state.
[/list]

[h2]How to play[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Land:[/b] give an airborne aircraft one waypoint near an airfield on your own island.
[*][b]Launch:[/b] give a parked aircraft a new waypoint away from the island.
[*][b]Cancel:[/b] give a new order before touchdown.
[/list]

[h2]Required: CC2X SDK 0.8.0 client beta 1[/h2]
[url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3833014670]Subscribe to the shared CC2X SDK[/url] as well as this mod. An SDK subscription downloads the runtime; install its bootstrap once:
[olist]
[*]Close Carrier Command 2. In the SDK's downloaded Workshop folder, open [b]content[/b].
[*]Copy [b]dinput8.dll[/b] next to [b]carrier_command.exe[/b] in the game folder. Back up an older identified CC2X DLL first; check compatibility before replacing any other loader.
[*]Enable Island Airfields in the game's Mods menu and restart.
[/olist]
The SDK Workshop folder is [code]steamapps/workshop/content/1489630/3833014670/content[/code]
A ModLoader build must explicitly support this exact SDK runtime before it can install it automatically. Older SDK versions do not provide the incoming-order capability required by this update.

[h2]Multiplayer beta scope[/h2]
Ordinary-host gameplay and the corrected map indicators passed the author's manual tests. [b]A second remote client and dedicated servers have not yet been verified.[/b] A remote-host capability/occupancy handshake is not implemented. These limits also apply to the Multiplayer Update cover image; it is not a claim of completed network acceptance.

[h2]Compatibility and feedback[/h2]
Windows, reviewed Carrier Command 2 1.5.18-r2 client. This mod changes screen_holomap.lua and screen_vehicle_control.lua; other changes to those screens need a compatible merge. Aircraft move between landing areas and hangar bays; full taxiing is not implemented. Include game/SDK versions, enabled mods, reproduction steps and cc2x.log with reports.

